# Analyst stage configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values:   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored; this template is not. The Analyst reads its variables,
# and the local Artifactory publishing tool reads only its variables. IA2 and
# IA3 need no credentials at all.
#
# Precedence: CLI flag > exported environment variable > `.env`.

# --- Model and credential --------------------------------------------------
#
# Any litellm model string works; see https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers
# for the format. Anthropic direct is the package default.

INSIGHT_AGENT_MODEL=
INSIGHT_AGENT_API_KEY=
INSIGHT_AGENT_API_BASE=

# --- Internal Artifactory publishing --------------------------------------
#
# Used only by `uv run tools/publish_artifactory.py`. The URL is the PyPI upload
# endpoint, not the `/simple` package index URL.

ARTIFACTORY_PYPI_URL=
ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN=

# --- Alternatives ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# OpenAI direct:
#   INSIGHT_AGENT_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.2
#   INSIGHT_AGENT_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# Bedrock:
#   INSIGHT_AGENT_MODEL=bedrock/anthropic.claude-opus-5
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible gateway — set an api_base alongside an `openai/` model
# prefix. Note that litellm strips the FIRST `openai/` to select the provider,
# so a gateway whose own model names already start with `openai/` needs it
# twice. `--dry-run` prints the assembled string before anything is spent.
#
#   INSIGHT_AGENT_API_BASE=https://your-gateway.example.com/v1
#   INSIGHT_AGENT_MODEL=openai/your-model-name
#   INSIGHT_AGENT_API_KEY=...

# INSIGHT_AGENT_API_BASE=

# OPENAI_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_BASE / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY are also honoured as
# fallbacks, so an environment already set up for litellm needs no changes.
